node_modules/
dist/
# The eye-test bench: its SOURCE is versioned in place, everything it GENERATES is
# not. The recipe in docs/contributing/manual-checks.md cannot run without the
# wiring and the views, and a `git clean` used to take them with the rest. Tracking
# them also settles what the ignore-in-full was guarding: shiki reads any
# non-authoring entry of `git status` as implementation in flight, and it is the
# UNTRACKED node_modules/ and .tgz that would gate a contract, never a committed
# .view. Editing one mid-contract IS authoring, and reads as such.
sandbox/*
!sandbox/.claude/
sandbox/.claude/*
!sandbox/.claude/settings.json
!sandbox/views/
sandbox/views/*
!sandbox/views/*.view
# Session state (mode locks, gate baselines, run results), never a contract.
# Globbed, not anchored: shiki resolves `.tayomi/` from the directory it is
# handed, so any folder a gate ever ran in acquires one holding nothing else.
**/.tayomi/state/
# The inbox is session state too, and the same rule reaches it: a contract is a
# decision the repo answers for, where this is a scratch list that empties as the
# session goes. Tracked, every line taken out of it became a commit of its own,
# and the file's whole history is a record of what was pending on a Sunday.
**/.tayomi/reminders.md
